Z||000003||Shiner||05-10-2000||12:55 PM||||I never sat in a rex, but my friend had a first gen, bought it when it was new.  He is a pretty tall person, around 6'1", maybe 180lbs.  He actually had to order leather seats in it because it gave him just MILLIMETERS of headliner clearence.  He said his head was on the roof with the cloth seats.  Intresting.  Now me, I am 6'3", 250lbs.  I don't think I could fit in that car!  Even if I could, I bet it would have that "fat old guy in a Geo Metro" look.  Not that I am fat and old.  <BR> My '87 GT fits me perfectly.  For some reason, my '84 (soon to be my mother's) is too small for me.  The seats seem to be up higher.  Weird.||||reg||1
